WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.658
Support needs boundaries or it will drown your delivery time.

00:00:03.658 --> 00:00:06.218
This lesson is about support without drowning.

00:00:06.218 --> 00:00:07.315
Boundaries and FAQs.

00:00:07.315 --> 00:00:09.876
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:13.533
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:19.020
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:23.043
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.043 --> 00:00:27.432
Stay practical: draft FAQ for buyers before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:27.752 --> 00:00:33.512
Draft an FAQ for buyers: common questions, response windows, and what is out of scope.

00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:36.200
Remember the objective: draft FAQ for buyers.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.424
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:40.424 --> 00:00:45.032
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:45.032 --> 00:00:49.256
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:49.256 --> 00:00:53.864
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.864 --> 00:00:56.552
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.552 --> 00:00:58.088
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:58.408 --> 00:00:59.950
